00:20:34.150 --> 00:20:39.270
You mostly are going to be directed to a holding area with some folding chairs in it.
你大部分时间都会被带到一个放着几把折叠椅的休息区。

447
00:20:39.370 --> 00:20:42.410
But my experience was there were never enough chairs for each person.
但根据我的经验，椅子从来都不够每个人坐的。

448
00:20:42.590 --> 00:20:44.570
Never enough chairs, and they're usually outside.
永远没有足够的椅子，而且通常都在户外。

449
00:20:44.990 --> 00:20:45.210
Yeah.
是啊。

450
00:20:45.730 --> 00:20:50.230
So Jenny said that when she first went to the wardrobe tent, she was given an apron to wear,
所以珍妮说，她第一次去服装帐篷时，发给她一件围裙穿，

451
00:20:50.350 --> 00:20:52.030
and she said she would be a grill cook.
而且她说她想应聘烤肉厨师。

452
00:20:52.190 --> 00:20:57.670
But then about an hour later, production pulled her aside and made her a Buffalo branch employee.
但大约一个小时后，制片组把她拉到一边，让她成了水牛城分公司的员工。

453
00:20:57.930 --> 00:21:01.750
And then they winked and said, you're going to be part of a special branch.
然后他们眨了眨眼，说你会加入一个特殊的部门。

454
00:21:02.030 --> 00:21:03.710
But she didn't know what that meant yet.
但她当时还不知道那是什么意思。

455
00:21:03.810 --> 00:21:04.030
Oh.
噢。

456
00:21:04.150 --> 00:21:05.370
And get this.
你听这个。

457
00:21:05.750 --> 00:21:11.970
Jenny talked to a bunch of the background folks, and she said that most of them were not
珍妮跟一帮群演聊过，她说他们大多数人

458
00:21:11.970 --> 00:21:17.130
office fans, that they had never seen the show, and that a few of them did not know who Steve
都不是《办公室》的粉丝，他们从没看过这部剧，而且其中几个人甚至不知道史蒂夫

459
00:21:17.130 --> 00:21:17.790
Carell was.
卡瑞尔是谁。

460
00:21:18.090 --> 00:21:24.110
She said they were thrilled to be working on our show because we had a reputation for treating
她说他们很高兴能参与我们的剧，因为我们以对待

461
00:21:24.110 --> 00:21:27.890
background performers very, very well and for providing great food.
群演非常非常好、提供极好的食物而闻名。

462
00:21:27.890 --> 00:21:34.030
She said one person told her from a work perspective, to be able to be an extra on the office for an
她说有人告诉她，从工作的角度来看，能在《办公室》里当一周的

463
00:21:34.030 --> 00:21:36.250
entire week, I feel like I won the lottery.
群演，感觉就像中彩票一样。

464
00:21:36.510 --> 00:21:39.310
So that made me really proud that our show did a good job.
所以这让我为我们的剧表现出色而感到非常自豪。

465
00:21:39.310 --> 00:21:45.090
Because as a person who did a lot of background work, it meant a lot.
因为作为一个曾经做过很多群演的人，这意义重大。

466
00:21:45.470 --> 00:21:49.970
Usually the background performers were like the last people who get to go through the lunch line,
通常群演就像是最后去排队吃午餐的人，

467
00:21:49.970 --> 00:21:52.330
and it's like what's left, almost nothing.
而且基本上只剩下残羹冷炙，几乎什么都没有了。

468
00:21:52.330 --> 00:21:54.970
And you were not allowed to go to craft services.
而且你们不准去剧组餐车区。

469
00:21:55.350 --> 00:22:02.350
But on our show, we had a whole buffet set aside just for the background performers and a whole craft
但在我们的剧组，我们专门为群演准备了整个自助餐区，还有一个一直保持

470
00:22:02.350 --> 00:22:04.930
services table that they kept full.
满满当当的剧组餐车桌。

471
00:22:05.070 --> 00:22:06.190
And it was awesome.
这太棒了。

472
00:22:06.190 --> 00:22:08.190
Well, you know, that's Randy Cordray.
你知道的，那是兰迪·科德雷。

473
00:22:09.130 --> 00:22:10.730
Randy took care of everyone.
兰迪照顾到了每一个人。

474
00:22:11.190 --> 00:22:14.910
However you were a part of our show, he was going to make sure you were taken care of.
无论你以什么身份参与我们的剧，他都会确保你被照顾得周到。

475
00:22:15.230 --> 00:22:16.670
That is absolutely true, lady.
千真万确，女士。

476
00:22:17.250 --> 00:22:18.050
All right, lady.
好吧，女士。

477
00:22:18.250 --> 00:22:19.490
Those are all my fast facts.
以上就是我的全部快速爆料。

478
00:22:19.630 --> 00:22:20.410
I mean, it's a lot.
我是说，内容挺多的。

479
00:22:20.750 --> 00:22:22.110
Well, it's a huge episode.
对啊，这是一集大体量的内容。

480
00:22:22.290 --> 00:22:22.670
I know.
我知道。

481
00:22:23.090 --> 00:22:23.690
All right.
好的。

482
00:22:23.830 --> 00:22:27.730
Should we take a break and then start breaking down this episode?
我们要不要休息一下，然后开始剖析这一集？

483
00:22:28.070 --> 00:22:28.630
Just heads up.
先提醒大家一下。

484
00:22:28.710 --> 00:22:29.610
It's going to be a long one.
这一集会很长。

485
00:22:29.950 --> 00:22:30.870
That's what she said.
她也这么说过。

486
00:22:31.090 --> 00:22:44.100
We are back, and the phone is ringing at reception.
我们回来了，前台的电话正在响。

487
00:22:44.500 --> 00:22:45.760
The lights are out.
灯都灭了。

488
00:22:46.060 --> 00:22:46.360
Yeah.
对。

489
00:22:46.500 --> 00:22:53.440
Erin takes the call, and she says that Michael is not in right now, but he'll call this person
艾琳接了电话，她说迈克尔现在不在，不过等他回来后

490
00:22:53.440 --> 00:22:54.580
back when he gets back.
会给这个人回电话。

491
00:22:54.720 --> 00:22:55.380
When he wakes up.
等他醒来后。

492
00:22:55.440 --> 00:22:56.080
I mean, gets back.
我是说，回来后。

493
00:22:56.180 --> 00:22:56.360
Right.
没错。

494
00:22:56.980 --> 00:22:57.700
Well, guess what?
你猜怎么着？

495
00:22:58.080 --> 00:23:00.580
Michael's sleeping because he had chicken pot pie for lunch.
迈克尔在睡觉，因为他午饭吃了鸡肉锅派。

496
00:23:00.660 --> 00:23:01.740
Not just chicken pot pie.
不只是鸡肉锅派。

497
00:23:02.240 --> 00:23:05.020
Jenna, he had the whole entire chicken pot pie.
珍娜，他吃了一整整个鸡肉锅派。

498
00:23:05.120 --> 00:23:07.580
A family-sized chicken pot pie.
一个家庭装的鸡肉锅派。

499
00:23:07.880 --> 00:23:10.020
And he's gone to sleep, as one would do.
然后他睡着了，这也是正常人会做的事。

500
00:23:10.280 --> 00:23:15.980
Well, the whole office is going to prank Michael into thinking that it is 5 o'clock when he
整个办公室都要恶作剧捉弄迈克尔，让他以为现在已经下午5点

501
00:23:15.980 --> 00:23:17.980
wakes up so that they can all go home early.
醒来，这样他们就能提前回家了。

502
00:23:18.280 --> 00:23:22.340
And Dwight does not normally condone leaving early, but he does have that appointment with
德怀特通常不赞成提前离开，但他今天确实和他的兽医有预约，

503
00:23:22.340 --> 00:23:24.240
his horse doctor today, so he's in.
所以他同意了。

504
00:23:24.640 --> 00:23:24.940
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

505
00:23:25.320 --> 00:23:27.040
Fan catch from Marcy G.
来自康涅狄格州的

506
00:23:27.460 --> 00:23:28.020
in Connecticut.
玛西·G的粉丝发现。

507
00:23:28.020 --> 00:23:31.560
There is a small detail that tickles me every time I see it.
有一个小细节每次看到都会让我忍俊不禁。

508
00:23:31.700 --> 00:23:36.660
In the cold open when they're tricking a sleeping Michael into thinking it's 5 p.m., they have
在冷开场里，当他们合伙欺骗正在睡觉的迈克尔，让他以为已经是下午5点时，他们得

509
00:23:36.660 --> 00:23:38.120
to change the time on his watch.
改掉他手表上的时间。

510
00:23:38.380 --> 00:23:41.640
Pam has her shoes off so she doesn't make noise in his office.
帕姆脱了鞋，这样她在他的办公室里就不会发出声音。

511
00:23:41.640 --> 00:23:48.040
But if you notice, Dwight also has his shoes off while he runs outside to change the time on
但如果你注意的话，德怀特在跑出去修改

512
00:23:48.040 --> 00:23:48.880
Michael's car.
迈克尔车上的时间时也脱了鞋。

513
00:23:49.080 --> 00:23:49.940
I saw that.
我注意到了。

514
00:23:50.080 --> 00:23:51.740
Jim also has his shoes off.
吉姆也脱了鞋。

515
00:23:51.760 --> 00:23:52.080
Yes.
是的。

516
00:23:52.280 --> 00:23:52.680
I don't know.
我不知道。

517
00:23:52.720 --> 00:23:54.680
Did everyone just take their shoes off?
大家是都把鞋脱了吗？

518
00:23:54.680 --> 00:23:59.200
We had another fan catch from Lloyd C.
我们收到了另一位来自澳大利亚的

519
00:23:59.540 --> 00:24:03.260
from Australia, who said, during Jim's talking
劳埃德·C的粉丝发现，他说在吉姆的

520
00:24:03.260 --> 00:24:09.320
head, when he goes to turn the clock forward, the time starts on 12.50.
单人访谈中，当他去把时钟往回拨时，时间是从12点50分开始的。

521
00:24:09.600 --> 00:24:15.880
But when Dwight goes to Michael's car to change the time, it starts at 12.10.
但当德怀特去迈克尔的车上改时间时，时间是从12点10分开始的。

522
00:24:16.140 --> 00:24:18.800
He said, was this a continuity gap?
他说，这是一个穿帮吗？

523
00:24:18.920 --> 00:24:22.800
Or did Dwight's Panther speed turn time backwards outside of the office?
还是说德怀特的“黑豹”速度把办公室外面的时间给倒转了？

524
00:24:22.800 --> 00:24:25.700
I think it was probably just a continuity catch.
我觉得这可能只是个连戏细节。

525
00:24:25.980 --> 00:24:30.520
You know, maybe they had originally intended to see Dwight running outside to the car first
你知道的，也许他们原本打算先拍德怀特跑出去到车里的镜头，

526
00:24:30.520 --> 00:24:33.740
and then have Jim explain it in his talking head.
然后让吉姆在单人访谈里解释。

527
00:24:34.160 --> 00:24:36.120
And then maybe they just swapped it in editing.
然后可能是在剪辑时把顺序调换了。

528
00:24:36.380 --> 00:24:39.580
I bet that's right, because Veda would have been all on top of this.
我敢说肯定是这样，因为维达对这些向来抓得极严。

529
00:24:39.700 --> 00:24:44.080
She had everything meticulously time-coded every time we had a clock.
我们每次出现时钟镜头，她都会一丝不苟地做好时间码记录。

530
00:24:44.120 --> 00:24:46.160
She was very, like, particular.
她特别……怎么说呢，极其讲究。

531
00:24:46.400 --> 00:24:48.300
So I feel like that was a change-up in editing.
所以我感觉这是剪辑时做的调整。

532
00:24:48.620 --> 00:24:51.740
Jenny Tan, who was there that day watching us film,
珍妮·谭，那夭在现场看着我们拍摄的人，

533
00:24:51.740 --> 00:24:58.860
noted that John had a really hard time winding the clock backwards and delivering his monologue
提到约翰在把时钟往回拨、说台词

534
00:24:58.860 --> 00:25:00.520
and timing it out perfectly.
并完美掌控时间方面遇到了很大困难。

535
00:25:00.760 --> 00:25:02.540
I thought so watching it.
我看着的时候也这么觉得。

536
00:25:02.660 --> 00:25:04.000
I'll tell you why.
我来告诉你为什么。

537
00:25:04.380 --> 00:25:06.700
John is so effortless as Jim.
约翰演吉姆时总是那么游刃有余。

538
00:25:06.940 --> 00:25:11.700
But in this moment, I could see him concentrating on that clock.
但在这一刻，我能看出他在全神贯注地对付那个时钟。

539
00:25:11.860 --> 00:25:14.320
And just for a split second, I thought I saw John.
就那么短短的一瞬间，我觉得我看到了约翰本人。

540
00:25:14.320 --> 00:25:21.660
Well, she said that the knob on the back was really, really tiny and that John kept overshooting the time.
嗯，她说后面的那个旋钮真的非常非常小，约翰总是把时间拨过头。

541
00:25:21.840 --> 00:25:27.100
Like, it kept ending on, like, 5.15 or 5.10 instead of right before 5.
比如，时间老是停在5点15分或者5点10分左右，而不是刚好在5点之前。

542
00:25:27.460 --> 00:25:32.220
But she said they finally got it perfect on the last take and then they stopped.
但她说他们在最后一条终于拍完美了，然后就收工了。

543
00:25:32.380 --> 00:25:33.380
They were like, we got it.
他们当时就说，搞定收工。

544
00:25:33.440 --> 00:25:34.000
Yeah, done.
对，完成了。

545
00:25:34.000 --> 00:25:40.280
Well, this whole elaborate ruse ends when they all collectively, on the count of three, just erupt into laughter.
好吧，这个精心策划的恶作剧在一声令下数到三时，大家齐声大笑中结束了。

546
00:25:40.780 --> 00:25:42.140
And this wakes Michael up.
这把迈克尔吵醒了。

547
00:25:42.280 --> 00:25:45.020
He laughs, too, because he always wants to be in on the joke.
他也跟着笑，因为他总想参与到大家的笑话中。

548
00:25:45.100 --> 00:25:45.860
Yes, yes.
对，对。

549
00:25:45.960 --> 00:25:47.020
But you had to be there.
但你得身临其境才懂。

550
00:25:47.180 --> 00:25:47.980
You had to be there.
你得身临其境才懂。

551
00:25:48.080 --> 00:25:49.500
It was a geography joke.
这是一个地理笑话。

552
00:25:49.740 --> 00:25:52.720
And then Michael sees the clock and does exactly what they hoped for.
然后迈克尔看到了时钟，做出了他们期望的反应。

553
00:25:52.800 --> 00:25:54.000
He's like, well, let's all go home.
他就像是在说，好吧，大家回家吧。

554
00:25:54.000 --> 00:25:59.840
I had a teeny tiny catch on Pam's desk at 1 minute 33 seconds when we're all laughing.
在1分33秒我们都在笑的时候，帕姆的桌子上有一个极小的瑕疵。

555
00:26:00.500 --> 00:26:09.240
I noticed, and I had forgotten this, that she has a Pratt mug on her desk that is what is holding all of her pens and pencils.
我注意到——我都忘了这事——她的桌上有一个普拉特学院的马克杯，里面插着她所有的钢笔和铅笔。

556
00:26:09.680 --> 00:26:12.180
And then she has her pink mug that she's drinking out of.
然后她手里拿着她喝水的粉色马克杯。

557
00:26:12.440 --> 00:26:14.520
But I spotted that Pratt mug.
但我发现了那个普拉特学院的马克杯。

558
00:26:14.700 --> 00:26:14.980
Aw.
噢。

559
00:26:14.980 --> 00:26:17.780
That's a great detail from our set decoration crew.
那是我们布景道具组的一个绝佳细节。

560
00:26:18.040 --> 00:26:19.020
Well, I love that.
噢，我很喜欢这个。

561
00:26:19.020 --> 00:26:25.720
I was way in the corner, back by Stanley's file cabinet, and that was just trying to get me in the shot.
我当时在最角落里，靠着斯坦利的档案柜后面，那只是为了把我拍进镜头里。

562
00:26:26.020 --> 00:26:27.640
Ken Quapis had me come out from accounting.
肯·夸皮斯让我从会计部走出来。

563
00:26:27.800 --> 00:26:28.860
Once again, I'm standing.
又一次，我站着。

564
00:26:29.140 --> 00:26:29.380
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

565
00:26:29.780 --> 00:26:31.600
And that's how we could all be there.
这就是我们大家都能出现在那里的原因。

566
00:26:31.900 --> 00:26:35.500
Well, now we have our super short opening credits.
好了，现在我们有了超级简短的片头。

567
00:26:35.780 --> 00:26:37.480
They are, like, 10 seconds.
它们大概只有10秒钟。

568
00:26:37.960 --> 00:26:43.740
Jen Salata did an interview with Office Tally, and she said they cut the credits down to get more time for the episode.
詹·萨拉塔接受了Office Tally的采访，她说他们缩短片头是为了给正片腾出更多时间。

569
00:26:44.060 --> 00:26:48.660
She mentioned that they had gone back and forth about maybe making this episode an hour.
她提到，他们曾反复讨论过是否要把这一集做成一个小时。

570
00:26:49.020 --> 00:26:51.080
But she said they didn't feel like they needed it.
但她说他们觉得没那个必要。

571
00:26:51.280 --> 00:26:59.240
There were other season finales, like The Job or Goodbye, Toby, where they had, like, tons of plot points to wrap up and huge moves they were going to make.
还有其他的季终集，比如《工作》或《再见，托比》，里面有成吨的剧情需要收尾，还有重大的转折要发生。

572
00:26:59.480 --> 00:27:03.760
But in this episode, she said they didn't have that much.
但在这一集里，她说过的内容没那么多。

573
00:27:03.760 --> 00:27:10.020
They just had kind of the one big move with Jim and Pam and a little bit of a move for Michael and Holly.
他们只有关于吉姆和帕姆的一个重大转折，以及迈克尔和霍莉的一点点进展。

574
00:27:10.280 --> 00:27:13.020
And then the rest of us, just little nods to our storylines.
至于我们其他人，就只是对各自故事线的一些小小呼应。

575
00:27:13.200 --> 00:27:13.440
Yeah.
是的。

576
00:27:13.700 --> 00:27:17.460
But she said they did need to steal that little bit of time from the credits.
但她说他们确实需要从片头里偷出那一小段时间。

577
00:27:17.460 --> 00:27:19.140
The day has arrived.
这一天终于来了。

578
00:27:19.140 --> 00:27:21.720
It is the Dunder Mifflin Company Picnic.
这就是邓德米夫林公司野餐会。

579
00:27:22.000 --> 00:27:25.960
Here's a breakdown of all the different branches and their t-shirts.
这里是各个分公司及其文化衫的详细列表。

580
00:27:26.320 --> 00:27:26.700
Oh!
哦！

581
00:27:27.100 --> 00:27:28.240
Thank you, Dunderpedia.
谢谢你，邓德百科。

582
00:27:28.380 --> 00:27:30.800
I started making notes, and then I saw you had it.
我开始做笔记，然后我发现你已经有了。

583
00:27:31.420 --> 00:27:33.660
So I'm going to read what you have.
所以我要念一下你整理的内容。

584
00:27:33.920 --> 00:27:45.940
Corporate Black t-shirts, Akron Yellow, Albany Light Blue, Buffalo Orange, Nashua Green, Rochester Dark Purple, Scranton Red, and Utica Dark Blue.
公司总部黑T恤、阿克伦黄、奥尔巴尼浅蓝、布法罗橙、纳舒厄绿、罗切斯特深紫、斯克兰顿红，以及尤蒂卡深蓝。

585
00:27:45.940 --> 00:27:49.900
Lady, I'm calling this episode The Plain Hats Club.
女士，我把这一集叫做“素色帽子俱乐部”。

586
00:27:50.200 --> 00:27:56.360
Oh, I can't wait to hear this, because I have some lingo I made up for this episode as well.
哦，我等不及要听这个了，因为我为这一集也发明了一些行话。

587
00:27:56.500 --> 00:27:59.160
Everyone in this episode is wearing a plain hat.
这一集里的每个人都戴着一顶素色帽子。

588
00:27:59.300 --> 00:28:06.540
And that is because if you wear a logo anywhere on your shirt or your hat, the production has to get it cleared with that company firSt.
那是因为如果你的衬衫或帽子上有任何标志，剧组必须先获得该公司的批准。

589
00:28:06.860 --> 00:28:10.440
So I have a breakdown of everyone's plain hat.
所以我有一份每个人的素色帽子清单。

590
00:28:10.740 --> 00:28:12.520
Like the plain baseball hats?
就像那种素色棒球帽吗？

591
00:28:12.520 --> 00:28:12.980
Yes!
对的！

592
00:28:13.500 --> 00:28:16.640
Jim is wearing a plain black baseball hat.
吉姆戴着一顶素色黑色棒球帽。

593
00:28:16.820 --> 00:28:18.320
Pam has a white visor.
帕姆戴着一个白色遮阳帽。

594
00:28:18.720 --> 00:28:24.180
Dwight has a tan fishing hat, which I googled and I learned is called a bucket hat.
德怀特戴着一顶棕褐色渔夫帽，我通过谷歌搜索得知这叫盆帽。

595
00:28:24.560 --> 00:28:24.820
Hmm.
嗯。

596
00:28:25.420 --> 00:28:28.020
Kevin is also wearing a tan bucket hat.
凯文也戴着一顶棕褐色盆帽。

597
00:28:28.480 --> 00:28:30.620
Angela has a floppy sun hat.
安吉拉戴着一顶宽檐遮阳帽。

598
00:28:31.200 --> 00:28:33.440
Andy has a tan Panama hat.
安迪戴着一顶棕褐色巴拿马帽。

599
00:28:33.960 --> 00:28:37.060
Aaron has a sort of light purple baseball hat.
阿伦戴着一顶类似于浅紫色的棒球帽。

600
00:28:37.680 --> 00:28:39.640
Creed has a light tan baseball hat.
克里德戴着一顶浅棕褐色的棒球帽。

601
00:28:39.640 --> 00:28:41.840
Ryan has a white visor.
瑞安戴着一顶白色遮阳帽。

602
00:28:42.100 --> 00:28:44.520
Stanley has a straw sun hat.
斯坦利戴着一顶草编太阳帽。

603
00:28:45.360 --> 00:28:50.620
Phyllis has no hat while she's playing volleyball, but she has a straw sun hat on the sidelines.
菲莉丝打排球时没戴帽子，但在场边时她戴着一顶草编太阳帽。

604
00:28:51.160 --> 00:28:52.420
Meredith has no hat.
梅雷迪思没戴帽子。

605
00:28:53.080 --> 00:28:54.480
Oscar has no hat.
奥斯卡没戴帽子。

606
00:28:55.120 --> 00:28:59.860
Charles Minor has a black Nike visor.
查尔斯·迈纳戴着一顶黑色耐克遮阳帽。

607
00:29:00.040 --> 00:29:01.340
How did we get away with that?
我们当时怎么能蒙混过关的？

608
00:29:01.380 --> 00:29:02.340
I don't know!
我不知道！

609
00:29:02.340 --> 00:29:06.020
Because it's Idris, and we're just like, let Idris do what he wants to do.
因为那是伊德瑞斯，我们当时就觉得，让伊德瑞斯做他想做的事吧。

610
00:29:06.320 --> 00:29:07.760
We're just glad to have you back.
你能回来我们太高兴了。

611
00:29:07.980 --> 00:29:08.860
I don't know.
我不知道。

612
00:29:09.780 --> 00:29:12.980
Toby also has a yellow baseball hat with a logo.
托比也戴着一顶带标志的黄色棒球帽。

613
00:29:13.040 --> 00:29:15.720
It has little trees, but I couldn't read what it was.
上面有小树的图案，但我看不清写的是什么。

614
00:29:15.980 --> 00:29:20.060
Well, you know, part of the hat strategy was because it got so hot during the day.
嗯，你知道的，帽子策略的一部分是因为白天太热了。

615
00:29:20.260 --> 00:29:21.280
We needed it.
我们需要它。

616
00:29:21.280 --> 00:29:27.340
We needed it when we were playing volleyball as well to kind of create a shade on our faces
我们打排球时也需要它，好在脸部制造一点阴影，

617
00:29:27.340 --> 00:29:32.500
so that you could see our expressions so we weren't completely blown out by the sun.
这样你们就能看到我们的表情，不至于被阳光完全刺得睁不开眼。

618
00:29:32.600 --> 00:29:34.020
Also for sun protection.
也是为了防晒。

619
00:29:34.340 --> 00:29:37.720
But you might notice that Michael and Holly do not wear hats.
但你可能会注意到迈克尔和霍利没有戴帽子。

620
00:29:37.900 --> 00:29:43.320
They are mostly in their cutesy little, like, love nest shady area.
他们大部分时间都待在他们那个可爱的小爱巢阴凉区里。

621
00:29:43.820 --> 00:29:44.480
Yeah, exactly.
对，没错。

622
00:29:44.840 --> 00:29:46.760
Well, Jenna, I also did a little bit of tracking.
对了，珍娜，我还做了一点追踪调查。

623
00:29:46.760 --> 00:29:52.540
I want you to know that I feel like this episode really brings out some of our characters' other traits.
我想让你知道，我觉得这一集真的很能展现我们某些角色的其他特质。

624
00:29:52.980 --> 00:29:53.480
Oh.
哦。

625
00:29:53.660 --> 00:29:54.500
I made a liSt.
我列了个清单。

626
00:29:54.760 --> 00:30:08.080
We have Sporty Pam, Saucy Jim, Petty Charles, Trash-Talking Andy, Snarky Michael, and my most favorite, Vacation Stanley.
我们有运动型帕姆、风骚型吉姆、小肚鸡肠的查尔斯、满嘴垃圾话的安迪、尖酸刻薄的迈克尔，还有我最喜欢的度假斯坦利。

627
00:30:08.340 --> 00:30:10.740
I love Vacation Stanley.
我太喜欢度假斯坦利了。

628
00:30:11.500 --> 00:30:14.060
So the picnic starts with Pam and Jim.
所以野餐从帕姆和吉姆开始。

629
00:30:14.060 --> 00:30:20.140
They're walking up, and they share a little bit about what last year's softball company picnic was like.
他们走过来，分享了一点去年公司垒球野餐的情况。

630
00:30:20.340 --> 00:30:24.280
Jim had that spider in his mitt, but that's not what Pam is talking about.
吉姆的手套里有那只蜘蛛，但帕姆说的不是这个。

631
00:30:24.500 --> 00:30:28.380
She's talking about the guy who grabbed her boobs to keep his balance.
她说的是那个为了保持平衡而抓她胸部的家伙。

632
00:30:28.940 --> 00:30:29.600
Uh-huh.
嗯哼。

633
00:30:29.880 --> 00:30:34.680
And then Pam points at her chest and says, yeah, you don't grab these for balance.
然后帕姆指着自己的胸口说，对啊，你抓这个可不是为了保持平衡。

634
00:30:34.940 --> 00:30:36.740
And Jim goes, well.
然后吉姆说，呃。

635
00:30:37.080 --> 00:30:39.040
And this is Saucy Jim.
这就是风骚吉姆。

636
00:30:41.120 --> 00:30:45.720
Well, next up, Dwight arrives with his friend, Rolf.
接下来，德怀特和他的朋友罗尔夫到了。

637
00:30:45.940 --> 00:30:47.340
His best friend?
他最好的朋友？

638
00:30:47.760 --> 00:30:55.640
Who they met at a shoe store when Dwight overheard Rolf asking for a shoe that would increase his speed but not leave any tracks.
他们是在一家鞋店认识的，当时德怀特无意中听到罗尔夫在打听一双能增加速度却不留痕迹的鞋子。

639
00:30:55.900 --> 00:30:57.420
These two are made for each other.
这两个人简直天生一对。

640
00:30:57.720 --> 00:30:59.920
We had a fan question from David H.
我们收到了来自宾夕法尼亚州的

641
00:31:00.000 --> 00:31:00.660
in Pennsylvania.
大卫·H. 的粉丝提问。

642
00:31:00.900 --> 00:31:02.360
Who played Dwight's friend?
扮演德怀特朋友的是谁？

643
00:31:02.720 --> 00:31:04.940
Was he somehow related to the show already?
他之前就和这部剧有什么渊源吗？

644
00:31:04.940 --> 00:31:09.460
Guys, Rolf was played by the amazing James Urbaniac.
伙计们，罗尔夫是由优秀的詹姆斯·乌尔巴尼亚克饰演的。

645
00:31:09.620 --> 00:31:10.780
And get this, Ange.
你听好了，安吉。

646
00:31:10.880 --> 00:31:11.100
What?
什么？

647
00:31:11.340 --> 00:31:14.800
He auditioned and was called back for the role of Dwight.
他曾为德怀特这个角色参加试镜并被叫去复试。

648
00:31:15.160 --> 00:31:17.420
Well, that makes perfect sense to me.
嗯，这对我来说完全说得通。

649
00:31:17.460 --> 00:31:17.980
Doesn't it?
不是吗？

650
00:31:18.240 --> 00:31:21.220
He and Rain knew each other from their New York theater days.
他和雷恩从当年在纽约的戏剧界就认识了。

651
00:31:21.440 --> 00:31:26.540
And after Rain read this script, he called James and gave him a heads up.
在Rain看完这个剧本后，他给James打了个电话，提前跟他打了招呼。

652
00:31:27.020 --> 00:31:30.600
And he told Greg, you need to bring in James Urbaniac for this.
他告诉Greg，你得让James Urbaniak来演这个角色。

653
00:31:30.600 --> 00:31:37.260
Well, they knew him because they had auditioned him, so he went in to see Allison Jones, he read for the role, and he got the part.
嗯，他们认识他是因为之前试镜过他，所以他去见了Allison Jones，试了这个角色，然后就拿下了。

654
00:31:37.580 --> 00:31:46.440
Ken talked a little bit in the DVD commentary about just how perfectly cast James was and that for a guest star to come in on such a big episode,
肯在DVD评论音轨里稍微聊了一下James的选角是多么完美，作为一个客串演员加入这样一集重头戏，

655
00:31:46.980 --> 00:31:51.200
James just fit in so seamlessly you would have never known he had never been on the show before.
James融入得是如此天衣无缝，你根本不会觉得他以前没演过这个节目。

656
00:31:51.400 --> 00:31:56.200
That is just how organic his performance was and that he just crushed it.
他的表演就是那么自然流畅，而且他简直演绝了。

657
00:31:56.200 --> 00:32:01.240
Well, he's one of those guys who's been a working actor for a very, very long time.
嗯，他是那种当了很久很久的职业演员的人。

658
00:32:01.460 --> 00:32:07.160
And I feel like he's one of those people where you recognize him immediately from his body of work.
而且我觉得他是那种你光看他的作品就能立刻认出来的人。

659
00:32:07.160 --> 00:32:07.800
He's a pro.
他是个专业演员。

660
00:32:08.080 --> 00:32:10.740
We got this interesting letter from Jana M.
我们收到了来自爱尔兰梅奥郡韦斯特波特的Jana M.的一封有趣的信。

661
00:32:11.000 --> 00:32:13.240
in Westport County, Mayo, Ireland.
在韦斯特波特郡，梅奥，爱尔兰。

662
00:32:13.660 --> 00:32:14.440
Oh, wow.
哦，哇。

663
00:32:14.500 --> 00:32:16.020
We have letters from everywhere.
我们收到了来自世界各地的信件。

664
00:32:16.160 --> 00:32:17.340
This is so exciting to me.
这让我太兴奋了。

665
00:32:17.540 --> 00:32:20.980
You know, we added a feature on the website where you can say where you're writing from.
你知道的，我们在网站上加了一个功能，你可以标明你是从哪里写信来的。

666
00:32:21.240 --> 00:32:22.140
I love that.
我太喜欢这个了。

667
00:32:22.140 --> 00:32:26.380
I know, me too, because it's really fun to see how international the show is.
我知道，我也是，因为看到这个节目有多么国际化真的很有趣。

668
00:32:26.460 --> 00:32:26.700
I know.
我知道。

669
00:32:26.820 --> 00:32:30.780
Well, when we get mail here to Earwolf that I open, I can always see where people are from.
嗯，当我们在Earwolf收到我拆开的邮件时，我总能看到大家来自哪里。

670
00:32:30.920 --> 00:32:33.020
But before in emails, we weren't always sure.
但以前在电子邮件里，我们不总是那么确定。

671
00:32:33.320 --> 00:32:34.920
Here is what Jana said.
Jana是这么说的。

672
00:32:35.180 --> 00:32:46.480
Fun fact, James Urbaniak, the actor who played Dwight's best friend Rolf, whom he met in a shoe store, also played a shoe store employee with a foot fetish on Sex and the City.
趣事，饰演德怀特最好朋友罗尔夫的演员詹姆斯·乌尔比尼亚克——他们在鞋店相识——也曾在《欲望都市》中饰演过一个有足恋情结的鞋店员工。

673
00:32:47.120 --> 00:32:50.160
What is it about James Urbaniak in shoe stores?
詹姆斯·乌尔比尼亚克跟鞋店是怎么回事？

674
00:32:50.760 --> 00:32:51.800
That's really funny.
这真的很有趣。

675
00:32:51.800 --> 00:32:52.780
I think that's fun.
我觉得这很有意思。

676
00:32:52.980 --> 00:32:54.640
And now Christine B.
现在来自密西西比州的

677
00:32:54.940 --> 00:32:57.080
from Mississippi asked this.
Christine B.问了这样一个问题。

678
00:32:57.300 --> 00:33:02.780
I've heard that Rolf was introduced because Moe's was busy on Parks and Rec.
我听说罗尔夫这个角色的引入是因为莫在《公园与游憩》剧组太忙了。

679
00:33:02.980 --> 00:33:04.080
Is that true?
这是真的吗？

680
00:33:04.440 --> 00:33:06.220
Oh, savvy question.
哦，真是个刁钻的问题。

681
00:33:06.640 --> 00:33:07.660
It is true.
这是真的。

682
00:33:08.340 --> 00:33:18.780
You guys, originally, Moe's was supposed to come to the picnic with Dwight, and they called up Mike Schur, who was now running Parks and Rec.
各位，原本莫应该是和德怀特一起去野餐的，他们给当时正在负责《公园与游憩》的迈克·舒尔打了电话。

683
00:33:18.780 --> 00:33:25.580
And the week we shot Company Picnic, he was directing an episode of Parks and Rec, as well as running the show.
在我们拍摄《公司野餐》的那周，他既在导演一集《公园与游憩》，又在负责整个节目。

684
00:33:26.020 --> 00:33:27.860
And he was like, you guys, I can't do it.
他说，伙计们，我做不到。

685
00:33:27.920 --> 00:33:29.120
And I guess they begged him.
我猜他们当时还恳求过他。

686
00:33:29.340 --> 00:33:32.740
Like, Jen and Paul, they were like, please, you have to come be Moe's.
就像珍和保罗，他们说，求你了，你得来演莫。

687
00:33:32.740 --> 00:33:35.740
And he's like, you guys, I can't do it.
而他说，伙计们，我真的不行。

688
00:33:35.940 --> 00:33:38.240
I am running a whole other show now.
我现在正负责另一整部剧呢。

689
00:33:38.340 --> 00:33:38.780
Yes.
是的。

690
00:33:39.180 --> 00:33:42.340
And then, you know, we're going to have Mike on the show.
然后呢，你知道的，我们等下会请迈克来节目。

691
00:33:42.540 --> 00:33:43.200
I can't wait.
我等不及了。

692
00:33:43.340 --> 00:33:47.900
And he's going to tell us a little bit about how he also truly hated playing Moe's.
他会给我们讲讲他是多么真心实意地讨厌演莫这个角色。

693
00:33:48.320 --> 00:33:49.000
Hated it.
讨厌极了。

694
00:33:49.160 --> 00:33:49.880
Hated it.
讨厌透了。

695
00:33:49.880 --> 00:33:59.900
So I think he was, like, really happy that he had a good excuse to not be out in this field in his wool clothes for four days.
所以我猜他当时真的很庆幸自己有个好借口，不用穿着毛呢衣服在野地里待上四天。

696
00:34:00.120 --> 00:34:04.180
It also made sense to me that Dwight wouldn't have brought Moe's to the Company Picnic.
我觉得德怀特不会带莫去公司野餐也很合逻辑。

697
00:34:04.400 --> 00:34:08.680
And I love this twist that he's got this best friend.
而且我非常喜欢他居然有这么个好朋友的反转。

698
00:34:08.980 --> 00:34:09.280
Yeah.
是啊。

699
00:34:09.280 --> 00:34:18.200
You know, there's a deleted talking head that made me laugh, but also sad, where Michael says he usually brings the guy from his condo with him.
你知道的，有一个被删掉的采访片段让我笑了，但也觉得难过，迈克尔在里面说他通常会带他公寓里的那个家伙一起去。

700
00:34:18.620 --> 00:34:20.600
But this year, he came by himself.
但今年，他自己一个人来了。

701
00:34:21.840 --> 00:34:23.740
The guy from his condo.
他公寓里的那个家伙。

702
00:34:24.100 --> 00:34:24.620
Yeah.
对。

703
00:34:25.260 --> 00:34:29.080
Well, Rolf is going to appear in four episodes of The Office.
罗尔夫将在《办公室》里出演四集。

704
00:34:29.080 --> 00:34:30.480
This was his firSt.
这是他的第一集。

705
00:34:30.960 --> 00:34:32.140
We loved you, James.
詹姆斯，我们太喜欢你了。

706
00:34:32.300 --> 00:34:33.720
He was really fun to work with.
和他合作真的很有趣。

707
00:34:33.740 --> 00:34:34.140
So fun.
太有趣了。

708
00:34:34.980 --> 00:34:36.680
Now enters Holly.
现在霍莉登场了。

709
00:34:37.180 --> 00:34:39.380
Oh, and Michael sees her.
哦，迈克尔看到她了。

710
00:34:39.580 --> 00:34:41.120
And Kevin's like, there's Holly.
凯文就像是在说，霍莉在那儿。

711
00:34:41.320 --> 00:34:43.040
And Michael's like, oh, you know, we're just friends.
迈克尔就像是在说，哦，你知道的，我们只是朋友。

712
00:34:43.780 --> 00:34:48.300
There's a whole awkward greeting between Holly and her boyfriend, AJ, with Michael.
迈克尔和霍莉以及她的男友AJ之间有一场非常尴尬的打招呼。

713
00:34:49.120 --> 00:34:52.260
And Jenna, this begins, snarky Michael.
詹娜，这就开始了，刻薄的迈克尔。

714
00:34:52.620 --> 00:34:58.040
Steve does this thing as Michael I love so much, where he lets his hatred for someone just barely poke out.
史蒂夫饰演的迈克尔有一个我非常喜欢的举动，他让对某人的厌恶只流露出一点点。

715
00:34:58.260 --> 00:34:58.620
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

716
00:34:59.320 --> 00:35:02.240
So he says, hey, I could get you guys some lemonade.
所以他说，嘿，我可以给你们拿点柠檬水。

717
00:35:02.700 --> 00:35:04.700
Holly says, lemonade sounds great.
霍莉说，柠檬水听起来不错。

718
00:35:04.700 --> 00:35:05.800
Michael goes, okay.
迈克尔说，好的。

719
00:35:06.360 --> 00:35:08.640
AJ says, I'd love an iced tea, actually.
AJ说，其实我想喝冰茶。

720
00:35:08.840 --> 00:35:10.760
And Michael goes, you can go to hell.
迈克尔说，你可以见鬼去了。

721
00:35:11.260 --> 00:35:12.060
Just kidding.
开玩笑的。

722
00:35:12.260 --> 00:35:12.780
Just kidding.
开玩笑的。

723
00:35:14.710 --> 00:35:16.590
He'll get him the best iced tea in the world.
他会给他拿世界上最好的冰茶。

724
