talk about Michael and Holly and what they're up to?
就聊聊迈克尔和霍莉以及他们在忙些什么？

1045
00:49:12.890 --> 00:49:13.310
Yeah.
好啊。

1046
00:49:13.550 --> 00:49:16.430
I think we need to come back and talk about some chair pants.
我觉得我们回来后得聊聊椅子裤的事。

1047
00:49:17.090 --> 00:49:17.790
Oh, great.
哦，太棒了。

1048
00:49:28.580 --> 00:49:29.560
We're back.
我们回来了。

1049
00:49:29.980 --> 00:49:32.960
And also, Snarky Michael is with us.
而且，刻薄的迈克尔也和我们在一起。

1050
00:49:33.160 --> 00:49:36.300
He gets a big piece of news here.
他在这里得到了一个重大消息。

1051
00:49:36.460 --> 00:49:37.560
He really does.
他的确是。

1052
00:49:37.560 --> 00:49:38.580
Bless his heart.
真善良。

1053
00:49:38.920 --> 00:49:41.880
They tell him that they're designing a house.
他们告诉他他们在设计一栋房子。

1054
00:49:42.120 --> 00:49:43.500
And he says, for who?
然后他问，为谁设计的？

1055
00:49:43.500 --> 00:49:46.680
And AJ says, for us.
AJ说，为我们。

1056
00:49:47.940 --> 00:49:52.600
And then Michael says, well, wow, I'm designing a chair.
然后迈克尔说，哇，我正在设计一把椅子。

1057
00:49:52.800 --> 00:49:54.000
It's part of your pants.
它是你裤子的一部分。

1058
00:49:54.160 --> 00:49:54.840
You sit down.
你坐下来。

1059
00:49:55.020 --> 00:49:55.520
You're supported.
你就能得到支撑。

1060
00:49:56.860 --> 00:49:58.360
Holly lights up.
霍莉眼睛一亮。

1061
00:49:58.820 --> 00:50:02.460
She's like, I remember your chair pants idea.
她说，我记得你那个裤子椅子的点子。

1062
00:50:02.920 --> 00:50:04.660
And AJ's like, I like that.
AJ说，我挺喜欢那个。

1063
00:50:04.740 --> 00:50:05.640
Put me down for a pair.
给我也留一条。

1064
00:50:05.760 --> 00:50:07.120
I'm a size 34 waiSt.
我腰围34码。

1065
00:50:07.640 --> 00:50:09.040
Here comes Snarky Michael.
尖酸刻薄的迈克尔登场了。

1066
00:50:09.540 --> 00:50:10.840
He can't take it anymore.
他再也忍不下去了。

1067
00:50:11.060 --> 00:50:12.180
He says, all right, fatty.
他说，好吧，大胖子。

1068
00:50:12.380 --> 00:50:13.160
I will do it.
我来做。

1069
00:50:13.160 --> 00:50:13.800
You know what?
你知道吗？

1070
00:50:14.220 --> 00:50:15.840
We should actually rehearse.
我们其实应该排练一下。

1071
00:50:16.020 --> 00:50:18.340
He wants to get Holly away from AJ.
他想把霍莉从AJ身边支开。

1072
00:50:18.760 --> 00:50:21.280
And AJ says, you guys are really going to do this?
AJ说，你们俩真的要这样做吗？

1073
00:50:21.320 --> 00:50:23.440
And Michael says, you bet your fat ass we are.
迈克尔说，你个大屁股，我们当然要做。

1074
00:50:24.220 --> 00:50:31.240
Because he can't contain how much he's freaking out that this guy has just swooped in and is
因为这家伙突然横插一脚，把他的挚爱给

1075
00:50:31.240 --> 00:50:32.840
taking the love of his life.
抢走了，他急得快要崩溃，根本按捺不住。

1076
00:50:32.840 --> 00:50:33.820
To build a house.
去盖房子。

1077
00:50:33.900 --> 00:50:34.580
To build a house.
去盖房子。

1078
00:50:34.680 --> 00:50:35.300
To build a home.
去建立一个家。

1079
00:50:35.460 --> 00:50:36.440
To become a family.
去组成一个家庭。

1080
00:50:37.480 --> 00:50:43.420
Well, we have this really sweet talking head where Michael and Holly together explain that David
好吧，我们有一段非常温馨的访谈，迈克尔和霍莉在其中一起解释说，大卫

1081
00:50:43.420 --> 00:50:49.820
Wallace has authorized them to perform a presentation on the history of Dunder Mifflin.
华莱士授权他们做一个关于邓德米夫林历史的演讲。

1082
00:50:49.820 --> 00:50:52.460
Again, David Wallace, what are you thinking?
话说回来，大卫·华莱士，你在想什么呢？

1083
00:50:52.940 --> 00:50:53.700
I don't know.
我不知道。

1084
00:50:54.500 --> 00:50:58.000
Well, Holly and Michael are going to find a nice little quiet place to rehearse.
好吧，霍莉和迈克尔要去找个安静惬意的地方排练了。

1085
00:50:58.480 --> 00:51:01.000
He brought her chocolate-covered strawberries.
他给她带了巧克力草莓。

1086
00:51:01.440 --> 00:51:04.720
When I rewatched this with my kids, they were like, wow.
当我陪着孩子们重温这段时，他们说，哇。

1087
00:51:05.100 --> 00:51:07.540
Because I think they associate this with Valentine's.
因为我觉得他们把这和情人节联系在了一起。

1088
00:51:08.080 --> 00:51:12.120
When you go to the grocery store, there's always a big chocolate-covered strawberry display for
每到情人节你去杂货店时，

1089
00:51:12.120 --> 00:51:12.900
Valentine's.
总能看到一大片巧克力草莓的展台。

1090
00:51:12.980 --> 00:51:14.320
It's a very romantic gift.
这是一份非常浪漫的礼物。

1091
00:51:14.500 --> 00:51:15.220
It is.
确实如此。

1092
00:51:15.340 --> 00:51:16.900
What snacks do you bring to a picnic?
你野餐会带什么零食？

1093
00:51:17.200 --> 00:51:21.540
You bring like potato chips, some salsa, chocolate-covered strawberries.
你会带薯片、莎莎酱、巧克力草莓之类的。

1094
00:51:21.860 --> 00:51:26.620
By the way, I love that your picnic items are potato chips and salsa.
顺便说一句，我真没想到你的野餐食品居然是薯片和莎莎酱。

1095
00:51:27.020 --> 00:51:28.220
I love chips and salsa.
我很喜欢薯片和莎莎酱。

1096
00:51:28.340 --> 00:51:31.040
I have never brought potato chips and salsa.
我从来没带过薯片和莎莎酱去野餐。

1097
00:51:31.380 --> 00:51:32.940
You don't like chips and salsa?
你不喜欢薯片和莎莎酱吗？

1098
00:51:33.240 --> 00:51:33.860
But don't you?
难道你不是吗？

1099
00:51:33.940 --> 00:51:36.780
You eat corn chips or like tortilla chips.
你吃的是玉米片或者玉米薯片之类的。

1100
00:51:36.780 --> 00:51:37.700
Okay, I'm sorry.
好吧，对不起。

1101
00:51:37.880 --> 00:51:42.140
But also, I've never brought salsa to like a picnic blanket.
而且，我从来没带过萨尔萨辣酱去野餐垫那种地方。

1102
00:51:42.340 --> 00:51:43.420
It's so messy.
太容易弄脏了。

1103
00:51:43.620 --> 00:51:45.560
Like the chips, yeah.
比如薯片之类的，对吧。

1104
00:51:45.820 --> 00:51:49.160
But like I don't bring dips to a picnic.
但我觉得我不会带蘸酱去野餐。

1105
00:51:49.500 --> 00:51:51.600
I don't think dip when I think picnic.
我一想到野餐就不会想到蘸酱。

1106
00:51:51.840 --> 00:51:57.900
Lady, lady, when my husband first came home with me to meet my family, my mom said to him,
天哪，天哪，当我丈夫第一次带我回家见我家人时，我妈妈对他说过，

1107
00:51:58.100 --> 00:51:59.040
we're dippers and chippers.
我们是无酱不欢、无薯片不欢的人。

1108
00:52:00.040 --> 00:52:00.600
Okay.
好吧。

1109
00:52:01.280 --> 00:52:06.320
We always have some kind of dip and something like a chip to eat it with.
我们总是备有某种蘸酱和用来蘸着吃的薯片之类的东西。

1110
00:52:06.320 --> 00:52:07.500
Even on your picnics?
连野餐也是这样吗？

1111
00:52:07.800 --> 00:52:09.600
Most definitely on a picnic.
野餐绝对也是这样。

1112
00:52:09.940 --> 00:52:10.300
Okay.
好吧。

1113
00:52:10.880 --> 00:52:13.240
It just seems like a mess waiting to happen.
这简直就像是随时会发生的一场灾难。

1114
00:52:13.380 --> 00:52:14.460
Give me all the dips.
把所有的蘸酱都给我吧。

1115
00:52:14.780 --> 00:52:15.440
All right.
好吧。

1116
00:52:15.720 --> 00:52:17.280
And, you know, bring some paper towels.
而且，你知道，带点纸巾就行了。

1117
00:52:18.020 --> 00:52:24.140
Well, I have something crazy to share about this location where they shot these Michael and Holly scenes.
嗯，关于拍摄迈克尔和霍莉这些场景的这个地方，我有个疯狂的内幕要分享。

1118
00:52:24.440 --> 00:52:24.980
The tree?
那棵树？

1119
00:52:25.180 --> 00:52:26.100
The little shady tree?
那棵阴凉的小树？

1120
00:52:26.260 --> 00:52:26.720
Yes.
对。

1121
00:52:27.040 --> 00:52:31.460
Randy said that this shaded location was the most troublesome of the whole shoot.
兰迪说这个有树荫的地方是整个拍摄过程中最麻烦的。

1122
00:52:31.460 --> 00:52:32.040
Why?
为什么？

1123
00:52:32.560 --> 00:52:38.400
He said, first off, they really wanted a romantic private area where these two could sneak off to,
他说，首先，他们非常想要一个浪漫而私密的地方，让这两个人可以偷偷溜过去，

1124
00:52:38.540 --> 00:52:41.320
but they still needed to feel the picnic in the background.
但他们又需要能感觉到背景里正在进行野餐。

1125
00:52:41.320 --> 00:52:41.700
Ah.
啊。

1126
00:52:41.920 --> 00:52:44.040
And it was really hard to find the right spot.
而且要找到合适的地方真的很难。

1127
00:52:44.700 --> 00:52:48.100
The one that they settled on drove Randall crazy.
他们最终选定的那个地方把兰德尔快折磨疯了。

1128
00:52:48.720 --> 00:52:56.080
I guess there were these overhanging trees, and then there was like a muddy creek where his lighting equipment needed to go.
我猜这里有一些悬垂的树木，然后还有一个泥泞的小溪，他的灯光设备必须架在那儿。

1129
00:52:56.080 --> 00:53:04.200
So, and we usually shot our show with just two cameras, but for this, they had to add a third camera.
所以，而且我们通常只用两台摄像机拍摄我们的节目，但为了这个，他们不得不增加第三台摄像机。

1130
00:53:04.380 --> 00:53:10.100
And it's because they just couldn't cover it with these over-the-shoulders.
这是因为他们光靠这些过肩镜头根本拍不全。

1131
00:53:10.220 --> 00:53:15.080
They looked good, but they really wanted a two-shot of them from the front.
这些镜头看起来不错，但他们真的很想要一个从正面拍他们的双人镜头。

1132
00:53:15.500 --> 00:53:18.560
But listen to this, and I barely understand how they did it.
但听着，我几乎搞不懂他们是怎么做到的。

1133
00:53:18.700 --> 00:53:18.940
Okay.
好吧。

1134
00:53:18.940 --> 00:53:27.380
It was so tight in this area that the only way that they could do it was they had to set up a mirror,
这个地方太狭窄了，他们唯一的办法就是架起一面镜子，

1135
00:53:27.380 --> 00:53:36.980
and they shot the camera into the mirror, and then in order to make it match the over-the-shoulder shots,
他们把镜头对着镜子拍，然后为了让它和过肩镜头匹配，

1136
00:53:37.180 --> 00:53:39.200
they reversed them in poSt.
他们在后期制作中将其反转了。

1137
00:53:39.640 --> 00:53:42.300
Because when they shot in the mirror, they were on the wrong sides.
因为当他们对着镜子拍摄时，他们站的位置左右颠倒了。

1138
00:53:42.600 --> 00:53:47.600
It was this, like, special mirror called, like, an optically correct mirror.
这是一种类似特殊镜子的东西，叫做光学矫正镜。

1139
00:53:48.100 --> 00:53:50.880
I barely understand this, but it was a huge ordeal.
我几乎听不懂这原理，但这真的是一个巨大的麻烦。

1140
00:53:51.440 --> 00:53:52.960
Well, it sounds like a huge ordeal.
嗯，听起来确实是个大麻烦。

1141
00:53:53.180 --> 00:53:58.260
I'm also very curious, could Steve and Amy see their reflections as they did the scene?
我也很好奇，史蒂夫和艾米在演这场戏时能看到自己的倒影吗？

1142
00:53:58.340 --> 00:53:59.320
Because that would be weird.
因为那会很奇怪。

1143
00:53:59.320 --> 00:54:01.420
I wouldn't, I don't want to watch myself, because then I'd be like,
我不会，我不想看自己，因为那样我就会想，

1144
00:54:01.440 --> 00:54:02.800
what are you doing with your face, lady?
大姐，你脸上在做什么表情？

1145
00:54:02.860 --> 00:54:03.500
What is that expression?
那是什么表情？

1146
00:54:03.500 --> 00:54:04.720
I would be so distracted.
我会彻底分心的。

1147
00:54:05.060 --> 00:54:05.400
Yeah.
是啊。

1148
00:54:06.440 --> 00:54:07.500
So, I don't know.
所以，我不知道。

1149
00:54:07.640 --> 00:54:11.580
My question was, like, did they just have this mirror on standby?
我的问题是，他们是刚好把这面镜子备用着吗？

1150
00:54:11.580 --> 00:54:12.880
Like, is that part of their kit?
就像，这是他们器材包里的标配吗？

1151
00:54:12.880 --> 00:54:17.660
They have an optically correct mirror in your camera kit.
你们的摄影器材里有一面光学正确的镜子。

1152
00:54:17.880 --> 00:54:18.760
I feel like that's a special order, lady.
我觉得这得特别定制吧，女士。

1153
00:54:18.980 --> 00:54:23.480
It sounds like a special order, but it also sounds like they kind of had to figure this out on the fly,
听起来像是特别定制的，但也听起来像是他们临时琢磨出来的，

1154
00:54:23.560 --> 00:54:25.640
but I don't know, maybe it was part of their planning scout.
不过我不知道，也许那是他们前期踩点计划的一部分。

1155
00:54:26.120 --> 00:54:29.040
Get that mirror in case we need it, and get a third camera.
带上那个镜子以防万一，再拿第三台摄像机。

1156
00:54:29.440 --> 00:54:31.760
You would have never known it by watching that scene, though.
不过看那场戏的时候，你绝对看不出来。

1157
00:54:31.880 --> 00:54:33.760
It was so beautiful and effortless.
它是那么优美、那么毫不费力。

1158
00:54:33.920 --> 00:54:36.980
I would have never known there was a mirror or a third camera.
我绝不会知道那里有一面镜子或第三台摄像机。

1159
00:54:37.440 --> 00:54:39.800
There's this great, great moment between Holly and Michael,
霍莉和迈克尔之间有一个非常、非常棒的时刻，

1160
00:54:39.800 --> 00:54:41.980
is they're brainstorming their ideas, right?
就是他们在头脑风暴他们的点子，对吧？

1161
00:54:42.540 --> 00:54:44.400
Yeah, they're going to do this skit,
对，他们打算演这个小品，

1162
00:54:44.480 --> 00:54:51.180
but this is the first time they've met to figure out the skit that's going to be going up soon.
但这是他们第一次碰面，来构思那个即将上演的小品。

1163
00:54:51.360 --> 00:54:52.680
And Michael has no script.
而且迈克尔没有剧本。

1164
00:54:52.860 --> 00:54:54.300
He just wants to wing it.
他只想临场发挥。

1165
00:54:56.200 --> 00:54:59.980
So, they start spitballing, like, movie spoofs, right,
所以，他们开始碰撞想法，比如电影恶搞，对吧，

1166
00:55:00.060 --> 00:55:03.860
to get out this information about how Robert Dunder and Robert Mifflin met.
来引出罗伯特·邓德和罗伯特·米夫林是如何相遇的信息。

1167
00:55:04.360 --> 00:55:06.060
Only part of it was scripted, Jenna.
只有一部分是写在剧本里的，珍娜。

1168
00:55:06.660 --> 00:55:11.000
Steve and Amy just improvised, and Ken said they love the improv.
史蒂夫和艾米完全是即兴发挥，肯说他们很喜欢这种即兴。

1169
00:55:11.160 --> 00:55:13.000
They just let the camera keep going and going.
他们就让摄像机一直拍一直拍。

1170
00:55:13.320 --> 00:55:13.580
Really?
真的吗？

1171
00:55:13.840 --> 00:55:14.160
Yes.
是的。

1172
00:55:14.280 --> 00:55:15.760
Here's how the scene started as written.
剧本里这场戏一开始是这样的。

1173
00:55:16.480 --> 00:55:18.300
Holly's like, what about Back to the Future?
霍莉说，回到未来怎么样？

1174
00:55:18.660 --> 00:55:19.020
Yeah.
对。

1175
00:55:19.600 --> 00:55:20.440
That was scripted.
那是剧本写好的。

1176
00:55:20.780 --> 00:55:22.180
The rest of this part was not.
这部分的其余内容则没有。

1177
00:55:22.340 --> 00:55:22.500
Ready?
准备好了吗？

1178
00:55:22.640 --> 00:55:22.700
What?
什么？

1179
00:55:22.940 --> 00:55:23.080
Yeah.
好。

1180
00:55:23.520 --> 00:55:24.760
How about Back to the Future?
回到未来怎么样？

1181
00:55:25.120 --> 00:55:27.800
Steve improvises, could we get a DeLorean?
史蒂夫即兴发挥，我们能弄来一辆德罗宁跑车吗？

1182
00:55:28.120 --> 00:55:28.660
So funny.
太搞笑了。

1183
