罗尔夫说，给你们出个会计问题。

1495
01:07:53.260 --> 01:07:55.720
What does one fiancé plus one lover equal?
一个未婚夫加上一个情人等于什么？

1496
01:07:56.080 --> 01:07:57.360
Answer, one whore.
回答，一个婊子。

1497
01:07:57.920 --> 01:08:00.060
Dwight says, okay, knock it off, Rolf.
德怀特说，行了，别闹了，罗尔夫。

1498
01:08:00.500 --> 01:08:01.440
Rolf says, what?
罗尔夫说，什么？

1499
01:08:01.440 --> 01:08:03.900
She's sitting here casting aspirations.
她坐在这里血口喷人。

1500
01:08:04.300 --> 01:08:06.140
And Dwight goes, Rolfard, please.
然后德怀特说，罗尔法德，拜托了。

1501
01:08:06.780 --> 01:08:10.840
Jenna, I swear I hear Dwight say, Rolfard, please.
珍娜，我发誓我听到德怀特说，罗尔法德，求你了。

1502
01:08:11.540 --> 01:08:14.340
Meaning like Rolfard is Rolf's full name?
意思是罗尔法德是罗尔的全名吗？

1503
01:08:14.540 --> 01:08:15.080
Yes.
对。

1504
01:08:15.660 --> 01:08:17.280
It's not documented anywhere.
任何地方都没有记录。

1505
01:08:17.280 --> 01:08:18.720
I'm probably just losing it.
可能是我疯了吧。

1506
01:08:18.880 --> 01:08:19.980
I need you to hear it.
我需要你也听听看。

1507
01:08:20.060 --> 01:08:20.700
I'm going to play it.
我要放出来了。

1508
01:08:20.860 --> 01:08:21.100
Ready?
准备好了吗？

1509
01:08:21.380 --> 01:08:21.640
Okay.
好。

1510
01:08:27.450 --> 01:08:28.590
Oh, okay.
哦，好吧。

1511
01:08:29.250 --> 01:08:30.250
Rolfard, please.
罗尔法德，求你了。

1512
01:08:30.250 --> 01:08:31.250
I'm telling you.
我跟你说真的。

1513
01:08:31.370 --> 01:08:31.610
Okay.
好吧。

1514
01:08:31.830 --> 01:08:34.070
Here's the first thing I need to know is this.
首先我要知道的是这个。

1515
01:08:34.070 --> 01:08:35.270
Is Rolf a name?
罗尔是一个名字吗？

1516
01:08:35.550 --> 01:08:36.470
That I don't know.
这个我不知道。

1517
01:08:36.530 --> 01:08:38.350
Did we make that up or is it a name?
这是我们编的还是本来就是个名字？

1518
01:08:38.730 --> 01:08:40.590
Is Rolf short for Rolfard?
罗尔是罗尔法德的简称吗？

1519
01:08:41.210 --> 01:08:44.310
Well, there's a restaurant in Manhattan called Rolf's.
曼哈顿有一家餐厅叫罗尔餐厅。

1520
01:08:44.490 --> 01:08:46.010
It's in Gramercy Park.
在格拉梅西公园。

1521
01:08:46.670 --> 01:08:48.310
Oh, here we go.
哦，开始咯。

1522
01:08:48.430 --> 01:08:48.910
Wikipedia.
维基百科。

1523
01:08:49.410 --> 01:08:50.010
Rolf.
罗尔。

1524
01:08:50.270 --> 01:08:52.510
It is a male given name and surname.
这是一个男性名字和姓氏。

1525
01:08:52.810 --> 01:08:56.710
It originates in the Germanic name Hrolf.
它起源于日耳曼语名字赫罗尔夫。

1526
01:08:57.290 --> 01:08:57.890
Interesting.
有意思。

1527
01:08:58.430 --> 01:09:00.350
But now Rolfard.
但现在是罗尔法德。

1528
01:09:01.370 --> 01:09:01.970
Rolfard.
罗尔法德。

1529
01:09:03.170 --> 01:09:05.930
We need background music for ladies who Google.
我们需要为搜索资料的女士们配点背景音乐。

1530
01:09:06.190 --> 01:09:07.150
We really do.
真的非常需要。

1531
01:09:08.490 --> 01:09:09.090
Okay.
好吧。

1532
01:09:09.090 --> 01:09:13.990
I will tell you, there is the Rolfard Leather Company in the UK.
我跟你说，英国有一家罗尔法德皮革公司。

1533
01:09:13.990 --> 01:09:16.730
They are a supplier of fine quality leathers.
他们是优质皮革的供应商。

1534
01:09:17.070 --> 01:09:23.970
Also, just from Ancestry.com, Michigan had the highest population of Rolfard families in 1880.
另外，根据 Ancestry.com 的数据，1880年密歇根州拥有最多的罗尔法德家族人口。

1535
01:09:24.270 --> 01:09:26.630
So I think you might be right.
所以我看你可能是对的。

1536
01:09:26.890 --> 01:09:28.670
Both names seem to be names.
这两个名字看起来都是真名字。

1537
01:09:29.030 --> 01:09:30.010
I mean, just come on.
我的意思是，拜托。

1538
01:09:30.010 --> 01:09:35.320
I think you're right.
我觉得你是对的。

1539
01:09:35.620 --> 01:09:38.360
I think we have broken a big case here.
我觉得我们在这里破了一桩大案。

1540
01:09:38.720 --> 01:09:41.340
Mom detectives, we declare Rolfard.
妈妈侦探，我们宣布罗尔法德成立。

1541
01:09:41.580 --> 01:09:46.160
Put it on your calendar that this is the first time Rolfard is being documented?
把这记在日历上，这是罗尔法德第一次被记录下来吗？

1542
01:09:46.480 --> 01:09:46.840
Yes.
是的。

1543
01:09:47.360 --> 01:09:48.880
In the office canon.
在《办公室》正史里。

1544
01:09:49.800 --> 01:09:50.280
Angela.
安吉拉。

1545
01:09:50.380 --> 01:09:51.180
I'm clapping for myself.
我在为自己鼓掌。

1546
01:09:51.260 --> 01:09:52.040
Applause for you.
为你鼓掌。

1547
01:09:52.480 --> 01:09:52.880
Thank you.
谢谢。

1548
01:09:53.060 --> 01:09:53.860
Good work.
干得好。

1549
01:09:54.060 --> 01:09:54.440
Thank you.
谢谢。

1550
01:09:54.600 --> 01:09:56.660
And now to whoever does subtitles, change it to Rolfard.
现在给做字幕的人，把它改成罗尔法德。

1551
01:09:56.760 --> 01:09:57.360
Thank you very much.
非常感谢。

1552
01:09:57.360 --> 01:10:02.440
I'd like to say that that was a combo mom detective, two ladies who Google move.
我想说这是一套“妈妈侦探”组合，两位女士的谷歌搜索大招。

1553
01:10:02.600 --> 01:10:05.360
Do you see how both of those came together?
你们看这两个情节是怎么完美融合到一起的吗？

1554
01:10:06.080 --> 01:10:07.120
It's beautiful, really.
真是太美妙了。

1555
01:10:07.260 --> 01:10:07.840
In that moment.
就在那个瞬间。

1556
01:10:07.980 --> 01:10:08.300
I do.
我懂。

1557
01:10:08.460 --> 01:10:09.160
I'm proud of us.
我为我们感到骄傲。

1558
01:10:09.980 --> 01:10:13.900
Ken shared that he really liked seeing Dwight softening to Angela.
肯分享说，他真的很喜欢看到德怀特对安吉拉态度软化。

1559
01:10:14.860 --> 01:10:16.520
Angela's clearly moved by this.
安吉拉明显被这一幕打动了。

1560
01:10:16.620 --> 01:10:20.300
And then right after the scene, there would have been an Angela talking head.
然后紧接着这个场景之后，本来应该有一段安吉拉的单人访谈。

1561
01:10:20.500 --> 01:10:22.440
It got deleted, but I wanted you to hear it.
这段被剪掉了，但我想让你们听听看。

1562
01:10:23.160 --> 01:10:26.640
Today, for the first time in months, Dwight nodded at me.
今天，几个月来第一次，德怀特对点了点头。

1563
01:10:27.240 --> 01:10:32.000
And I have to admit, it made my heart sit up just a little straighter in its chair.
我必须承认，这让我的心在胸膛里不由自主地挺直了腰板。

1564
01:10:32.340 --> 01:10:37.800
I know I seem hard and cold on the outside, but on the inside, I'm as warm as porcelain.
我知道我外表看起来坚强冷酷，但我的内心就像瓷器一样温暖。

1565
01:10:39.810 --> 01:10:41.790
I'm sorry for gushing on like this.
抱歉我这样滔滔不绝。

1566
01:10:43.270 --> 01:10:46.210
Just must be the apple juice talking or...
肯定是因为刚才喝了苹果汁，或者……

1567
01:10:46.210 --> 01:10:47.350
I don't...
我不知道……

1568
01:10:49.090 --> 01:10:50.170
It's very sweet.
这真的很甜。

1569
01:10:50.790 --> 01:10:53.550
She is as soft as porcelain on the inside.
她内心就像瓷器一样柔软。

1570
01:10:54.610 --> 01:10:56.530
Apple juice is not on the drink menu.
饮品菜单上可没有苹果汁。

1571
01:10:56.590 --> 01:10:57.790
I knew you were going to say that.
我就知道你会这么说。

1572
01:10:58.050 --> 01:11:02.890
I also now like this expression of saying, it just made my heart sit up a little straighter
我现在也很喜欢这种表达，说“让我的心在胸膛里不由自主地挺直了腰板”

1573
01:11:02.890 --> 01:11:03.470
in its chair.
。

1574
01:11:03.470 --> 01:11:04.430
I loved that too.
我也很喜欢这个。

1575
01:11:04.450 --> 01:11:05.630
I thought it was cute.
我觉得很可爱。

1576
01:11:05.810 --> 01:11:06.130
What?
什么？

1577
01:11:06.710 --> 01:11:10.950
The game is going and Pam is going to fall.
游戏开始了，帕姆要摔倒了。

1578
01:11:11.650 --> 01:11:13.330
Lady, I did my own falling stunt.
大姐，我可是自己完成的摔倒特技。

1579
01:11:13.490 --> 01:11:13.990
That's all me.
全是我自己演的。

1580
01:11:14.250 --> 01:11:15.190
I believed it.
我相信。

1581
01:11:15.270 --> 01:11:16.090
I'm very proud of it.
我对此非常自豪。

1582
01:11:16.250 --> 01:11:18.750
It's not the first time you fall in this episode.
这可不是你在这集里第一次摔倒。

1583
01:11:18.750 --> 01:11:19.710
You fall twice.
你摔了两次。

1584
01:11:19.930 --> 01:11:20.410
I do?
我有吗？

1585
01:11:20.410 --> 01:11:20.790
Yeah.
对啊。

1586
01:11:21.030 --> 01:11:26.970
You had a spontaneous fall while you were playing fake volleyball earlier in the episode.
你在这一集前面假装打排球时，来了一次即兴摔倒。

1587
01:11:27.170 --> 01:11:27.510
Oh.
哦。

1588
01:11:27.670 --> 01:11:28.470
I clocked it.
我注意到了。

1589
01:11:28.550 --> 01:11:30.430
You went down to your knees to get a ball.
你为了接球双膝跪地。

1590
01:11:30.850 --> 01:11:31.170
Huh.
哈。

1591
01:11:31.450 --> 01:11:31.750
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

1592
01:11:32.010 --> 01:11:32.910
I'm a pro.
我是专业的。

1593
01:11:33.130 --> 01:11:34.450
You are sporty, Pam.
你很有运动细胞，帕姆。

1594
01:11:35.250 --> 01:11:40.250
Well, there had been a lot of discussion about using my double and shooting the fall from behind,
好吧，之前大家讨论过用替身，从背后拍摄摔倒的镜头，

1595
01:11:40.250 --> 01:11:44.690
but Ken said to sell it, they really needed to see my face on camera.
但肯说为了卖力演出，镜头里真的必须看到我的脸。

1596
01:11:44.850 --> 01:11:46.550
And it wasn't the shoulder rotation.
而且这跟肩膀扭伤没关系。

1597
01:11:46.550 --> 01:11:50.030
Yes, there was no reason why they couldn't just have me fall.
对，完全没理由不让我亲自摔。

1598
01:11:50.270 --> 01:11:51.950
It was not going to affect my shoulder.
这不会影响我的肩膀。

1599
01:11:52.730 --> 01:11:58.950
Randy told me that sometimes in movies, they will use a stunt double from the front,
兰迪告诉我，有时候拍电影，他们会用正面的特技替身，

1600
01:11:58.950 --> 01:12:01.930
and then they do CGI face replacement.
然后用电脑特效换脸。

1601
01:12:02.230 --> 01:12:02.570
What?
什么？

1602
01:12:02.810 --> 01:12:03.010
Yeah.
对。

1603
01:12:03.450 --> 01:12:04.350
Is this face-off?
这是变脸对决吗？

1604
01:12:04.590 --> 01:12:07.690
Kind of, like the movie magic version of face-off.
有点像，电影《变脸》的魔法特效版。

1605
01:12:08.010 --> 01:12:09.610
He said we could not afford that.
他说我们负担不起那个。

1606
01:12:10.050 --> 01:12:13.370
So there was no putting my face on her face.
所以没能把我的脸换到她脸上。

1607
01:12:13.730 --> 01:12:14.070
Okay.
好吧。

1608
01:12:14.070 --> 01:12:19.930
So, you know, at the end of this, when Pam is going to leave to get her ankle checked,
所以，你知道的，在这个片段快结束时，当潘要离开去检查脚踝时，

1609
01:12:20.650 --> 01:12:22.550
Dwight has to start stalling for time.
德怀特得开始拖延时间。

1610
01:12:22.750 --> 01:12:26.370
And the first thing he does is he, like, kicks the volleyball really far away.
他做的第一件事就是，把排球踢得老远。

1611
01:12:26.530 --> 01:12:31.910
This reminded me of, like, the butthole kid growing up, like, when you played kickball,
这让我想起从小到大那种“讨厌鬼”，就是你踢球的时候，

1612
01:12:32.070 --> 01:12:34.490
who would have a tantrum and kick the ball real far.
会发脾气把球踢得超级远。

1613
01:12:34.650 --> 01:12:35.010
Totally.
完全是。

1614
01:12:35.010 --> 01:12:36.070
And someone had to go get it.
然后得有人去把球捡回来。

1615
01:12:36.070 --> 01:12:38.530
Well, we had a fan catch from Emily H.
嗯，我们收到了来自俄亥俄州的粉丝艾米丽·H.

1616
01:12:38.630 --> 01:12:40.270
in Ohio who said,
发来的消息，她说，

1617
01:12:40.810 --> 01:12:44.110
I have a background catch at 16 minutes 55 seconds.
我在16分55秒处发现了一个背景穿帮。

1618
01:12:44.310 --> 01:12:50.610
When Dwight kicks the volleyball away to stall the game, there are some weird face cutout board
当德怀特把排球踢开以拖延比赛时，背景里有一些奇怪的人形立牌

1619
01:12:50.610 --> 01:12:55.670
picture things in the background, and I think there is a person sticking their head through
拍照板之类的东西，我觉得有人把头伸进了

1620
01:12:55.670 --> 01:12:56.310
one of them.
其中一个洞里。

1621
01:12:56.450 --> 01:12:56.870
Really?
真的吗？

1622
01:12:56.870 --> 01:12:58.410
I saw those things.
我看到那些东西了。

1623
01:12:58.550 --> 01:12:59.970
They look like something from a carnival.
它们看起来像是嘉年华上的玩意儿。

1624
01:13:00.330 --> 01:13:00.850
All right.
好吧。

1625
01:13:01.050 --> 01:13:07.390
I don't know if this is related, but Jenny Tan wrote this in her diary for the day.
我不知道这有没有关系，但珍妮·谭在她当天的日记里写了这样的话。

1626
01:13:07.750 --> 01:13:08.490
She said,
她说，

1627
01:13:08.490 --> 01:13:13.430
During the first few takes of Dwight kicking the ball, there was a background performer
在德怀特踢球的前几次拍摄中，有一个背景演员

1628
01:13:13.430 --> 01:13:14.870
hiding in the shack.
藏在小屋里。

1629
01:13:15.930 --> 01:13:21.710
And whenever the volleyball was kicked near it, this person would wave his arm outside the
每当排球被踢到附近时，这个人就会在小屋外面

1630
01:13:21.710 --> 01:13:23.170
shack and ruin the take.
挥舞手臂，导致拍摄穿帮。

1631
01:13:23.690 --> 01:13:28.210
She said, needless to say, this person was asked to leave the set and was told not to
她说，不用说，这个人被请出了片场，并被告知这周剩下的时间

1632
01:13:28.210 --> 01:13:29.730
return for the rest of the week.
都不用来上班了。

1633
01:13:29.990 --> 01:13:30.910
I don't know.
我不知道。

1634
01:13:30.990 --> 01:13:31.790
What's happening?
发生什么事了？

1635
01:13:31.790 --> 01:13:32.610
I don't know.
我不知道。

1636
01:13:32.870 --> 01:13:37.610
I was like, could that be the person whose face was in the little, like, picture thing?
我在想，那会不会就是把脸凑在那个小相框里的人？

1637
01:13:37.610 --> 01:13:39.370
Well, you know I'm going to go back and look.
好吧，你知道我待会儿肯定要回去看一眼。

1638
01:13:39.530 --> 01:13:39.930
I know.
我知道。

1639
01:13:40.750 --> 01:13:44.230
Well, not in the shack, waving their arms, or Michael and Holly.
好吧，不是在小屋里挥舞手臂的，而是迈克尔和霍莉。

1640
01:13:44.330 --> 01:13:45.330
How's that for a transition?
这个转场怎么样？

1641
01:13:45.330 --> 01:13:46.590
That was a wonderful transition.
那是个绝妙的转场。

1642
01:13:46.870 --> 01:13:47.410
I like that.
我喜欢。

1643
01:13:47.710 --> 01:13:50.350
We should share with you guys, we often wonder how to transition.
我们应该和大家分享一下，我们经常在想该怎么做转场。

1644
01:13:51.650 --> 01:13:55.550
We are trying so hard not to have every transition be lady.
我们一直在努力，不想让每次转场都用“那么”。

1645
01:13:55.850 --> 01:13:56.910
Lady, our well.
“那么”，我们的口头禅。

1646
01:13:57.390 --> 01:13:57.790
Yes.
对。

1647
01:13:57.950 --> 01:13:58.650
Oh, the wells.
哦，那些“那么”。

1648
01:13:58.830 --> 01:13:59.190
The wells.
那些“那么”。

1649
01:13:59.330 --> 01:13:59.990
We do a lot of wells.
我们用了好多“那么”。

1650
01:14:00.250 --> 01:14:02.250
Dr. Peter Thibodeau, please don't count the wells.
彼得·蒂博多医生，请千万别数我们说了多少次“那么”。

1651
01:14:02.370 --> 01:14:02.870
Oh, don't.
噢，别这样。

1652
01:14:03.030 --> 01:14:06.410
Oh, I have Dr. Thibodeau a few times, and it was staggering.
噢，我有几次找过提博多医生，那感觉真是震撼。

1653
01:14:07.890 --> 01:14:14.110
Anyways, Michael and Holly are going to reflect on their skit and on their mistake of mentioning
不管怎样，迈克尔和霍莉要反思他们的滑稽短剧，以及他们提到

1654
01:14:14.110 --> 01:14:19.450
the buffalo thing, and they have this very sweet couplet of dialogue.
那头野牛的错误，他们有一段非常甜蜜的对话。

1655
01:14:20.430 --> 01:14:22.690
Holly says, well, I'm glad we did it.
霍莉说，好吧，我很高兴我们这么做了。

1656
01:14:23.130 --> 01:14:24.330
Michael says, me too.
迈克尔说，我也是。

1657
01:14:24.790 --> 01:14:29.990
And there's a long pause, and he says, we have a lot of good material for next year's
然后是一段长长的停顿，他说，我们为明年的

1658
01:14:29.990 --> 01:14:30.330
sketch.
短剧准备了好多精彩素材。

1659
01:14:30.810 --> 01:14:33.990
And she lights up and says, I can't wait.
她眼前一亮说，我等不及了。

1660
01:14:35.010 --> 01:14:38.450
Well, this was a really beautiful performance by Steve and Amy.
真的，这是史蒂夫和埃米非常精彩的一场表演。

1661
01:14:38.790 --> 01:14:43.810
They shared in the DVD that everyone at Video Village, where they were watching the playback,
他们在DVD里分享说，在“视频村”观看回放的每个人,

1662
01:14:43.990 --> 01:14:44.470
was crying.
当时都哭了。

1663
01:14:45.110 --> 01:14:47.270
They said Jenny was there, Jenny Tan.
他们说珍妮也在那儿，珍妮·陈。

1664
01:14:47.450 --> 01:14:48.110
She was crying.
她当时哭了。

1665
01:14:48.770 --> 01:14:54.130
And then Ken said something I just loved about this scene between Steve and Amy.
然后肯说了一句我特别喜欢的话，是关于史蒂夫和埃米这场戏的。

1666
01:14:54.270 --> 01:14:57.010
I wrote it down verbatim, and I want to read it to you.
我一字不差地记了下来，想读给你们听。

1667
01:14:57.210 --> 01:14:57.410
Okay.
好的。

1668
01:14:57.410 --> 01:15:02.250
Ken said, it's the toughest kind of scene, because in a way, everything is happening,
肯说，这是最难拍的一种戏，因为在某种程度上，万事皆在发生，

1669
01:15:02.410 --> 01:15:04.650
and nothing is happening all at once.
却又似乎什么都没发生。

1670
01:15:05.130 --> 01:15:10.510
There's a gigantic shift that takes place, but it's all under the surface, and the challenge
发生了一次巨大的转变，但这一切都在水面之下，而挑战

1671
01:15:10.510 --> 01:15:17.070
is to find it over and over again, take after take, as if they've never been there.
在于一遍又一本地去寻找它，就像他们从未经历过一样。

1672
01:15:17.630 --> 01:15:18.010
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

1673
01:15:18.690 --> 01:15:19.070
Yeah.
是啊。

1674
01:15:19.070 --> 01:15:23.090
I just thought that was really well said, because every time they did it, they had to
我只是觉得这段话讲得太好了，因为他们每次演的时候，都必须

1675
01:15:23.090 --> 01:15:28.110
have that discovery of knowing that something just changed for both of them.
去体会到那种“他们俩之间有些事情刚刚改变了”的发现感。

1676
01:15:28.490 --> 01:15:29.630
It's a beautiful scene.
这是一场美丽的戏。

1677
01:15:29.770 --> 01:15:30.030
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

1678
01:15:30.390 --> 01:15:31.530
And then they say goodbye.
然后他们道别了。

1679
01:15:31.770 --> 01:15:36.510
And then Michael has this fantastic talking head, where he says he didn't find the perfect
接着迈克尔有一个绝妙的单独访谈镜头，他说他今天没有找到

1680
01:15:36.510 --> 01:15:39.950
moment that day to share those things with her, but it's okay, because they're going
完美的时机跟她分享那些事情，但没关系，因为他们会成为那种有着漫长故事的情侣，而他会很有耐心。

1681
01:15:39.950 --> 01:15:44.370
to be one of those couples who have a long story, and he's just going to be patient.
他会很有耐心。

1682
01:15:44.370 --> 01:15:49.770
Yeah, Jen said in an interview that they loved setting up this idea that Michael was going
是啊，珍在采访中说过，他们很喜欢这样一种设定：迈克尔打算

1683
01:15:49.770 --> 01:15:53.530
to find a way at this picnic to try to make his move with Holly.
在这场野餐中找个机会向霍莉采取行动。

1684
01:15:53.870 --> 01:16:00.170
But then, over the course of the day, as he spent time with her, he was reminded that they
但后来，在这一天当中，随着他和她在一起的时间增加，他记起了他们

1685
01:16:00.170 --> 01:16:05.570
have something really special, and he gains this more mature way of looking at the relationship.
拥有非常特别的东西，于是他对这段关系有了更成熟的看法。

1686
01:16:06.070 --> 01:16:11.630
And it's very different than how he would behave if this were Jan or any other woman from
这与如果换作简或他过去的任何其他女性时他的表现大不相同，

1687
01:16:11.630 --> 01:16:19.590
his past, and that she said, quote, he was calm and confident and quieted by this thought.
她还说，原话是，“他很平静、很自信，这个想法让他安静了下来”。

1688
01:16:19.850 --> 01:16:21.370
And I loved that.
我太喜欢这个了。

1689
01:16:21.530 --> 01:16:21.950
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

1690
01:16:22.090 --> 01:16:28.530
And this talking head right here is why you know this is his soup snake.
而正是在这里的这个单独访谈镜头，让你知道这绝对是他的“心灵伴侣”。

1691
01:16:28.930 --> 01:16:29.570
Yeah.
是啊。

1692
01:16:29.870 --> 01:16:30.790
His soulmate.
他的灵魂伴侣。

1693
01:16:31.450 --> 01:16:31.670
Soup.
心“零”伴侣。

1694
01:16:32.250 --> 01:16:33.910
A hundred percent, right?
百分之百，对吧？

1695
01:16:34.470 --> 01:16:34.850
Yeah.
是啊。

1696
01:16:34.850 --> 01:16:43.470
Well, Jim is going to take Pam to a local hospital, and for whatever reason, they have this belief
接下来，吉姆要带帕姆去当地医院，不管出于什么原因，他们竟然

1697
01:16:43.470 --> 01:16:46.030
that Dwight can stall this volleyball game.
觉得德怀特能拖延这场排球比赛。

1698
01:16:46.210 --> 01:16:46.990
I mean...
我是说……

1699
01:16:46.990 --> 01:16:47.730
For how long?
能拖多久？

1700
01:16:47.790 --> 01:16:48.610
I mean, you...
我是说，你……

1701
01:16:48.610 --> 01:16:52.350
Have you ever gone to get an ankle checked or anything checked?
你有没有去检查过脚踝或做过什么检查？

1702
01:16:52.730 --> 01:16:57.370
Even just the commute and finding parking and getting inside and signing up and getting
光是通勤、找停车位、走进大楼、登记、核对

1703
01:16:57.370 --> 01:16:59.530
your insurance information and...
你的保险信息，还有……

1704
01:16:59.530 --> 01:17:00.210
I don't know.
我不知道。

1705
01:17:00.210 --> 01:17:06.610
Jim is feverishly filling out some hospital form while a sassy nurse is wheeling Pam away.
吉姆正在手忙脚乱地填写一张医院表格，而一个态度傲慢的护士正把帕姆用轮椅推走。

1706
01:17:07.090 --> 01:17:09.590
The sassy nurse was played by Allison Martin.
这个傲慢的护士由艾莉森·马丁饰演。

1707
01:17:09.890 --> 01:17:15.290
She's done a ton of television comedy, most recently Grace and Frankie, and she did an episode
她演过大量的电视喜剧，最近的是《同妻俱乐部》，她还演过一集

1708
01:17:15.290 --> 01:17:15.890
of Law and Order.
《法律与秩序》。

1709
01:17:16.190 --> 01:17:16.490
Oh.
哦。

1710
01:17:16.810 --> 01:17:18.850
We had a fan question from Christy H.
我们收到了来自马里兰州的克里斯蒂·H.

1711
01:17:18.970 --> 01:17:19.990
in Maryland who said,
的粉丝提问，她说，

1712
01:17:20.070 --> 01:17:24.550
My 13-year-old son thinks the hospital that Jim and Pam go to is the Scrubs Hospital.
我13岁的儿子觉得吉姆和帕姆去的医院就是《实习医生风云》里的那家医院。

1713
01:17:24.550 --> 01:17:25.470
Is he right?
他猜对了吗？

1714
01:17:25.470 --> 01:17:26.810
He's a huge Office fan.
他是《办公室》的超级粉丝。

1715
01:17:26.810 --> 01:17:28.310
And Sam O.
还有来自威斯康星州密尔沃基的

1716
01:17:28.530 --> 01:17:30.170
from Milwaukee, Wisconsin said,
萨姆·O.说，

1717
01:17:30.350 --> 01:17:34.910
At the end of this episode, you guys are clearly in the hospital from Scrubs.
这集快结束时，你们显然是在《实习医生风云》拍摄的那家医院取景。

1718
01:17:35.170 --> 01:17:37.270
Do you remember anything about working there?
你们还记得在那儿工作的事吗？

1719
01:17:37.450 --> 01:17:39.610
Was the cast of the other show around at all?
另一个剧组的演员当时在附近吗？

1720
01:17:39.810 --> 01:17:42.610
Well, I tell you what, Christy, your son is right.
好吧，我告诉你，克里斯蒂，你儿子猜对了。

1721
01:17:43.270 --> 01:17:44.470
Sam, you are right.
萨姆，你猜对了。

1722
01:17:44.890 --> 01:17:49.290
This was the hospital that they used on Scrubs.
这就是他们在《实习医生风云》里用过的医院。

1723
01:17:49.830 --> 01:17:51.470
It is a former hospital.
它曾经是一所医院。

1724
01:17:51.470 --> 01:17:52.870
It's not even around anymore.
现在已经不存在了。

1725
01:17:53.090 --> 01:17:53.910
They've torn it down.
他们已经把它拆了。

1726
01:17:53.910 --> 01:17:56.610
But at the time, it was an abandoned hospital.
但在当时，它是一座废弃的医院。

1727
01:17:56.610 --> 01:17:59.610
It was the Riverside Community Hospital in Sherman Oaks.
那是谢尔曼奥克斯的河滨社区医院。

1728
01:17:59.870 --> 01:18:02.150
The Scrubs cast were not there that day.
那天的《实习医生风云》剧组并不在那里。

1729
01:18:02.330 --> 01:18:08.310
But Randy told us that their production graciously allowed us to use some of their pre-dressed
但兰迪告诉我们，他们的剧组非常慷慨地允许我们使用他们一些已经布置好的

1730
01:18:08.310 --> 01:18:10.390
corridors and examination rooMs.
走廊和检查室。

1731
01:18:10.910 --> 01:18:16.710
And something I'll tell you is that we shot all of this hospital stuff on Monday.
我要告诉大家的是，我们所有这些医院的戏份都是在周一拍摄的。

1732
01:18:16.710 --> 01:18:18.730
It was our very first day of shooting.
那是我们拍摄的第一天。

1733
01:18:18.870 --> 01:18:21.430
It was before we ever went out to the company picnic.
那甚至是在我们去公司野餐之前。

1734
01:18:21.430 --> 01:18:25.330
So all of that emotion was just day one.
所以所有这些情绪都只是第一天发生的。

1735
01:18:25.470 --> 01:18:25.910
Day one.
第一天。

1736
01:18:26.110 --> 01:18:26.270
Wow.
哇。

1737
01:18:26.270 --> 01:18:30.010
We started with the cold open, and then we relocated to the hospital.
我们从冷场开场开始，然后转移到了医院。

1738
01:18:30.530 --> 01:18:35.850
And Jenny recalled that she was not allowed to observe the hospital.
珍妮回忆说，她不被允许去围观医院的戏份。

1739
01:18:36.110 --> 01:18:39.310
She knew that we were going to a hospital, but she didn't know why.
她知道我们要去医院，但她不知道原因。

1740
01:18:39.470 --> 01:18:41.870
And we'll tell you more about that in just a little bit.
我们待会儿会告诉你们更多关于这方面的事。

1741
01:18:42.130 --> 01:18:44.290
I don't know how much longer Dwight can stall.
我不知道德怀特还能拖延多久。

1742
01:18:44.490 --> 01:18:47.930
The corporate team is insisting that Scranton put in their subs.
公司团队坚决要求斯克兰顿提交替补名单。

1743
01:18:47.930 --> 01:18:52.630
And Dwight is doing this really long roundabout thing of like, well, how many people must get
而德怀特一直在绕着一个超级大的圈子，说什么，究竟要有多少人受伤

1744
01:18:52.630 --> 01:18:54.170
hurt before a lesson is learned?
才能吸取教训？

1745
01:18:54.330 --> 01:18:58.810
One, two, three, four.
一个、两个、三个、四个。

1746
01:18:59.130 --> 01:19:01.430
He's doing a horrible job of stalling.
他拖延的工作做得糟糕透顶。

1747
01:19:01.670 --> 01:19:03.730
But Jim is like, Dwight, keep stalling.
但吉姆的意思是，德怀特，继续拖延。

1748
01:19:03.830 --> 01:19:07.030
And then he gets called into the room where Pam is.
然后他被叫进了帕姆所在的房间。

1749
01:19:07.310 --> 01:19:09.790
And they get some pretty big news.
他们得到了一个相当重大的消息。

1750
01:19:09.970 --> 01:19:11.470
But we can't hear it.
但我们听不见。

1751
01:19:11.710 --> 01:19:12.190
Nope.
没有。

1752
01:19:12.470 --> 01:19:14.150
But I think we know what it is.
但我想我们都知道那是什么。

1753
01:19:14.250 --> 01:19:14.690
Yes.
是的。

1754
01:19:15.310 --> 01:19:16.350
We got some mail.
我们收到了一些邮件。

1755
01:19:16.810 --> 01:19:21.530
A lot of people wanted to know, why was this scene silent?
很多人想知道，为什么这个场景是静音的？

1756
01:19:22.550 --> 01:19:25.310
Obviously, they're being told that they're going to have a baby.
很显然，他们被告知他们要有一个孩子了。

1757
01:19:25.550 --> 01:19:26.710
Why couldn't we hear it?
为什么我们听不到声音？

1758
01:19:27.270 --> 01:19:30.430
Well, this was partially inspired by the British show.
嗯，这部分灵感来自于英国的那部剧。

1759
01:19:30.590 --> 01:19:35.730
There is a scene in that series where Tim is going to tell Dawn how he feels about her.
那部剧里有一个场景，蒂姆要告诉唐恩他对她的感觉。

1760
01:19:35.890 --> 01:19:37.810
But first, he takes off his microphone.
但首先，他摘下了麦克风。

1761
01:19:38.270 --> 01:19:43.730
And Jen and Paul thought that this made that moment even more intimate.
珍和保罗觉得这让那个时刻更加亲密。

1762
01:19:43.730 --> 01:19:47.110
It's one of those things, kind of like the teapot note.
这是那种事情之一，有点像茶壶便签。

1763
01:19:47.430 --> 01:19:54.110
There's nothing that you could write that could ever meet people's expectations of what
没有什么你能写的东西能够达到人们对它应有的期望。

1764
01:19:54.110 --> 01:19:55.270
it needed to be.
它需要成为的样子。

1765
01:19:55.450 --> 01:20:00.830
So if you leave it for people to fill in themselves, it'll always be the perfect note.
所以如果你让人们自己去填补，它永远会是完美的便签。

1766
01:20:01.070 --> 01:20:01.770
I agree.
我同意。

1767
01:20:01.770 --> 01:20:06.250
And I feel like Randall Einhorn shared with us that the further you were away from a moment,
我觉得兰德尔·埃因霍ーン跟我们分享过，你离一个时刻越远，

1768
01:20:06.410 --> 01:20:08.410
the more intimate it feels to watch.
观看时的感觉就越亲密。

1769
01:20:08.410 --> 01:20:09.030
Yeah.
对。

1770
01:20:09.490 --> 01:20:09.570
Yeah.
对。

1771
01:20:09.570 --> 01:20:12.130
And so removing the sound makes you pretty far away.
所以去掉声音会让你离得很远。

1772
01:20:12.490 --> 01:20:12.750
Yeah.
对。

1773
01:20:13.090 --> 01:20:16.750
Well, this idea was something we had been toying with for a long time.
嗯，这个想法我们已经琢磨很久了。

1774
01:20:16.930 --> 01:20:21.890
On casino night, there was a whole conversation about whether or not we should hear Jim tell
在赌场之夜，曾有过一场讨论，关于我们在停车场时是否应该听到吉姆告诉

1775
01:20:21.890 --> 01:20:25.330
Pam that he has feelings for her out in the parking lot.
帕姆他对她有感觉。

1776
01:20:25.510 --> 01:20:28.610
We ultimately decided to keep the audio for that.
我们最终决定保留那段音频。

1777
01:20:28.830 --> 01:20:32.550
But, you know, we're going to do this again when Pam says goodbye to Michael.
但是，你知道的，当帕姆向迈克尔告别时，我们要再做一次这个。

1778
01:20:32.550 --> 01:20:37.390
Every once in a while, it was a trick we could use because we were a documentary.
偶尔，这是我们可以使用的一个技巧，因为我们是一部纪录片。

1779
01:20:37.790 --> 01:20:40.810
We could pull the sound and make a really impactful moment.
我们可以抽离声音，造就一个极具冲击力的时刻。

1780
01:20:41.690 --> 01:20:44.230
So Jim is going to run into the hallway now.
所以吉姆现在要跑进走廊了。

1781
01:20:44.410 --> 01:20:48.690
He's going to call Dwight and he's going to say, send in the subs.
他要打电话给德怀特，并说，派替补上场。

1782
01:20:48.990 --> 01:20:49.930
We got mail.
我们有信了。

1783
01:20:50.870 --> 01:20:51.410
Annette E.
来自明尼苏达州的

1784
01:20:51.630 --> 01:20:52.770
from Minnesota said,
安妮特·E.说，

1785
01:21:09.370 --> 01:21:15.510
So, yeah, John Krasinski, man, why he didn't win an Emmy, why you didn't, why the whole freaking
所以，是的，约翰·卡拉辛斯基，老兄，他为什么没拿艾美奖，你为什么没有，为什么整个该死的

1786
01:21:15.510 --> 01:21:19.670
cast didn't win more awards because the show is delivering right here.
剧组没有赢得更多奖项，因为这部剧在这里表现太出色了。

1787
01:21:20.350 --> 01:21:24.590
Ken shared on the DVD commentary a note that he gave John for this scene.
肯在DVD评论音轨中分享了一个他在这个场景中给约翰的提示。

1788
01:21:24.810 --> 01:21:26.150
And I thought it was great.
我觉得这很棒。

1789
01:21:26.390 --> 01:21:28.030
And I want you guys to hear it.
我想让你们听听。

1790
01:21:28.490 --> 01:21:33.090
The one thing I told John to remember is that over the course of this series,
我告诉约翰要记住的一件事是，在这部剧的整个过程中，

1791
01:21:33.090 --> 01:21:38.610
he's developed a relationship with the documentary camera operator.
他与纪录片摄影师建立了一种关系。

1792
01:21:38.810 --> 01:21:42.830
And so when John emerges from the room to make the call to Dwight,
所以当约翰从房间里出来给德怀特打电话时，

1793
01:21:43.730 --> 01:21:49.470
something about seeing his pal, the cameraman, kind of suddenly got him very choked up.
看到他的老朋友摄影师，某种程度上突然让他感到非常哽咽。

1794
01:21:49.470 --> 01:21:50.470
Wow, what a great note.
哇，多棒的提示啊。

1795
01:21:50.970 --> 01:21:54.350
And it's like, look, yeah, that told me this look.
就像是，看，是的，这解释了那个眼神。

1796
01:21:54.630 --> 01:21:59.910
Because we debated whether or not he should be so wrapped up in the moment that he should ignore the camera.
因为我们曾讨论过他是否应该完全沉浸在当下而忽视镜头。

1797
01:22:00.050 --> 01:22:01.130
But in fact, it was the opposite.
但事实上，恰恰相反。

1798
01:22:01.330 --> 01:22:01.570
This look right there.
就是那里的那个眼神。

1799
01:22:01.950 --> 01:22:08.270
It was almost like, you know, the cameraman has been sharing so much of what's going on with Jim that,
这就好像，你知道的，摄影师一直分担着那么多吉姆正在经历的事情，

1800
01:22:08.330 --> 01:22:10.910
you know, that it became very important to acknowledge him here.
你知道的，在这里向他致意变得非常重要。

1801
01:22:12.090 --> 01:22:15.990
So the look he is talking about happens at 20 minutes, 50 seconds.
所以他谈论的那个眼神出现在第20分50秒。

1802
01:22:16.910 --> 01:22:20.990
And you guys know these moments in your life where you're feeling all of this emotion,
你们大家也知道生活中会有这种时刻，你百感交集，

1803
01:22:20.990 --> 01:22:22.750
and then you see a good friend.
然后你看到了一位好朋友。

1804
01:22:23.470 --> 01:22:25.990
And it just comes pouring out of you.
情绪就一下子喷涌而出了。

1805
01:22:26.230 --> 01:22:29.790
It's that person that says, are you okay, when you're not okay.
